LOCAL turn 3 Q: Write a Python function that checks whether a string is a palindrome. Give only the code.
LOCAL turn 3 A: ```python\ndef is_palindrome(s):\n    """\n    Checks whether a given string is a palindrome.\n\n    Args:\n        s: The input string.\n\n    Returns:\n        bool: True if the string is a palindrome, False otherwise.\n    """\n    # Convert to lowercase and remove spaces/punctuation if you want to check for\n    # alphanumeric palindromes strictly. For a direct check on the string as is,\n    # we just compare it with its reverse.\n    \n    # A common and simple approach:\n    return s == s[::-1]\n\n# Example usage:\n# print(is_palindrome("madam"))  # Output: True\n# print(is_palindrome("racecar")) # Output: True\n# print(is_palindrome("hello"))  # Output: False\n# print(is_palindrome("a"))      # Output: True\n```
